    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d563">

                <pb facs="0545" n="469" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg469"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Senate Doc. No. 324,</note>
                <note rend="inline" type="source">64th Congress, 1st sess.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The President’s message
                            transmitting to the Senate a report of the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#italic">To the Senate:</hi>
                </p>
                <p>In response to the resolution adopted by the Senate on January 6, 1916,
                    requesting the President to inform the Senate, if not incompatible with the
                    public interests, upon certain subjects respecting the situation in Mexico, and
                    to transmit to the Senate the documents, letters, reports, orders, and so forth,
                    therein referred to, I transmit herewith a report by the Secretary of State,
                    with accompanying papers.</p>
                <p>The report of the Secretary of State has my approval.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Woodrow Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <placeName type="venue"><hi rendition="#small-caps">The White
                                House</hi></placeName>, <lb/>
                            <placeName type="city"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1916-02-16"><hi rendition="#italic">February 17,
                        1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </closer>















